The 655k batch without LR scaling is a strong discard (`1.793275`): throughput stayed high, but only 533 updates undertrained the model. I’m testing the principled companion change before abandoning it—scale all peak learning rates by 1.25, matching the 1.25× larger batch so cumulative update and weight-decay magnitude approximate the 524k setup.
